    77	Accepts file paths, pytest node ids, bare function names and `Class.test_x`; resolves them by a
    78	static AST scan of `test_*.py` / `*_test.py` (never executes tests). A bare name defined in two
    79	files is **ambiguous** (candidates listed); an unknown name or path is an **error**. `match`
    80	compares two lists AFTER normalisation, so "the implementer wrote function names and the matcher
    81	compared paths" cannot happen again: both sides become node ids first.
    82	
    83	## Limitations (declared)
    84	
    85	- `approval_gate.py` decides on evidence it is GIVEN; it cannot verify that the reviewer really ran
    86	  or that `final_rev` is the revision on disk. The gate agent's prompt (above) and the launch ledger
    87	  (W1) bind the evidence to the run; W2's checkpoint binds phases to revisions.
    88	- `test_refs.py` recognises pytest/unittest shapes (module-level `test*` functions, `test*`
    89	  methods in classes). Parametrised ids (`test_x[case]`) are NOT normalised: the suffix is compared
    90	  literally and the reference comes back `node-not-found`.
    91	- Known-open, found by the cross-review rounds of the v1.4.1-rc.1 candidate (2026-09-18) and not
